WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.206 --> 00:00:02.047
-Guys, you may have heard
about this,

00:00:02.047 --> 00:00:04.267
but the website Yahoo! Answers
just announced

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:05.734
that they're shutting
down forever.

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:07.167
[ Audience groans ]

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:09.200
And it really -- it's really
difficult news,

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.968
because one of my favorite
groups is the Yahoo! --

00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:14.000
Yahoo! Answers lounge singers.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:17.300
They're one
of my favorite groups.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.367
They sing real Yahoo! Answers
submitted by real people.

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:22.234
So, if you don't mind,
I booked them on the show

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:23.868
to perform one last time.

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:26.567
Here they are, the
Yahoo! Answers lounge singers.

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:28.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:38.934
Hey, Ronda.

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:41.834
-Hi, Kad.
How's it going?

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:44.267
-Yeah. It's going great.

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:46.501
I got some questions
that need answered.

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:49.200
-Alrighty, well, I'm going
to see what I can do.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.367 --> 00:01:01.667
-♪ Can someone please give me a
Netflix username and password? ♪

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:04.501
-♪ Just give me $10 a month ♪

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:08.200
♪ And I'll give you my
name and password ♪

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:12.467
-Oh, hey, I like that answer.

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:15.234
-Yeah, I like that question.

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:18.501
-Alright.
Well, how about this one?

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:21.901
♪ Is Christian Bale
a Christian ♪

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:26.334
♪ Since his name is Christian? ♪

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:34.033
-♪ Is Mitt Romney
a baseball glove? ♪

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:36.667
-Now that --
now that is a good point.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:40.968
-Yeah,
that's a good point, Kas.

00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:42.400
-Kad.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.601
-Kad is my friend.

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:49.234
-This next one makes
a good point as well.

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:52.200
♪ Which is worse? ♪

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.567
♪ Ignorance or apathy ♪

00:01:56.567 --> 00:02:02.267
-♪ I don't know
and I don't care ♪

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:03.901
-Oh.

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:06.133
Ooh, ooh, ooh.

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:07.968
That -- that stings.

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:09.033
-Yeah, it stings.

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:12.000
It stings worse
than a shook up beehive.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.767
You know what that is.
-[ Laughs ] Yeah

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.167
-Yeah.
-You can say that again.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:17.200
-It's when you take a bunch
of bees and you shake them,

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.434
and the last one that stings
you, you got to marry him.

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:22.834
-Let's -- let's see how spicy

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:28.934
this next question is.

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:36.000
♪ How many fingers
am I holding up? ♪

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.033
♪ Depends... ♪

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:41.968
♪ Are you angry? ♪

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:44.667
-Oh.
[ Applause ]

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:46.534
I'm glad --

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:48.133
I'm glad you're here
to answer my questions.

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:51.501
-And I'm happy as pie
to be answering them,

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:53.300
and I think we
know what that means,

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:54.634
the saying.

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:56.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.133
[ Piano solo ]

00:02:58.133 --> 00:03:00.834
♪♪

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:02.767
Oh, get into it.

00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:07.901
♪♪

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:09.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:12.167
-I got another one for you.

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:18.200
-Lay it on me,
my inquisitive friend Kad.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:25.434
-♪ Why do chips get stale? ♪

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:34.100
-♪ Thog don't care ♪

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.133
-Thog? Thog wrote that?

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:37.501
-Classic Thog.

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:39.868
Thog wrote that indeed.

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:41.667
-I wonder if Thog
wrote this next one.

00:03:41.667 --> 00:03:45.567
-Oh. [ Giggles ]

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:52.501
-♪ How do you get YouTube
to come film you? ♪

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:54.734
-♪ Just keep on calling ♪

00:03:54.734 --> 00:04:00.767
♪ And soon they will respond ♪

00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:02.667
[ Laughs ]
-Wow.

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:05.100
-Yeah.
-That took a turn.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.734 --> 00:04:09.300
-You know, I just got
to find it sometimes, but I do.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.901
I do.
I find it in my own time.

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:13.534
-Yeah, you got it.

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:15.367
I got one more question,
if you've got some time.

00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:17.868
-Oh, yeah, I'm going nowhere.
I live here.

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:20.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:22.133
-Yeah?
-I live in here.

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:23.767
-Okay, perfect.

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:32.367
♪ Has anyone ever held their
breath for over an hour? ♪

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:34.901
-♪ Yes ♪

00:04:34.901 --> 00:04:40.834
♪ Dead people ♪

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:43.334
-That is all our time, folks.
Thanks for having us.

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:45.467
We'll be right back with more
of "The Tonight Show."

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:46.901
Why do I say that?

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:48.501
We're not on "The Tonight Show."

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:50.634
Oh, we are, we are!

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:52.267
Hey, Jimmy!
Hey, say hi.

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:53.801
-Oh, my gosh.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:04:53.801 --> 00:04:55.601
-I'm a big fan.

00:04:55.601 --> 00:04:58.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

